"otpauth text · plaintext" = "otpauth text · plaintext";
"privacy.scope.body" = "This notice applies to InkOTP on iOS and the InkOTP website and contact channels. You can use the app without an InkOTP account. It generates codes on your device. The developer cannot access the accounts, keys, codes, camera frames or backups you use in the app. InkOTP saves your choice about this notice on your device.";
"privacy.data.heading" = "On-device data and permissions";
"privacy.data.body" = "InkOTP uses the service name, account name, verification key and parameters you enter or import to manage your accounts and compute time-based codes. It saves account order, lock options and copy expiration locally.\n\nWhen you choose to scan a QR code and grant permission, the camera is used on the scan screen. InkOTP does not save camera frames. You can turn off camera access in Settings and still enter a key or select a photo. The app receives only the photo or document you select in the system picker. A cloud file provider may handle files you choose under its own policy.\n\niOS manages Face ID, Touch ID, passcodes and device authentication. InkOTP uses the authentication result and cannot access your biometric templates or passcode. The app hides vault content in the app switcher and during screen recording or mirroring. iOS still allows screenshots.\n\nWhen you copy a code, InkOTP places it on the local device pasteboard with the selected expiration. Device diagnostics show time, memory and local file size only on your device.";
"privacy.retention.heading" = "Storage, backups and deletion";
"privacy.retention.body" = "The encrypted vault is kept in the app's private storage and excluded from supported automatic backups. You can edit or delete accounts in InkOTP and export backups to a location you choose. Resetting or deleting the app removes its private files. Files you exported belong to you and remain at their chosen locations. Plaintext migration files include the verification keys.\n\nA lost device, forgotten recovery password or damaged backup may prevent recovery. InkOTP has no remote copy or recovery service.";
"privacy.components.heading" = "On-device components";
"privacy.components.body" = "InkOTP uses Apple system frameworks for the interface, QR recognition, device authentication and encryption. The bundled Argon2 and scrypt code derives encryption keys on the device. InkOTP has no advertising, analytics, tracking, crash reporting or remote account sync.";
"privacy.website.heading" = "Website and email";
"privacy.website.body" = "When you visit the InkOTP website or contact the developer, hosting, security and email providers may process data needed to serve pages, protect services or respond to your request. Please keep keys, codes, passwords, backups and screenshots containing them out of messages to the developer.";
"privacy.rights.heading" = "Your choices and rights";
"privacy.rights.body" = "You can manage accounts on your device, revoke camera access in iOS Settings, and withdraw your consent in InkOTP Settings. Withdrawing locks the app and leaves the encrypted vault on your device. You can exercise applicable privacy rights or report a privacy concern by contacting the developer.";
"privacy.changes.heading" = "Children and updates";
"privacy.changes.body" = "InkOTP is for a general audience. Use it with a guardian's consent and guidance where the law requires it. Material changes to this notice will be announced and, where needed, presented for consent again.";
